Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue, but it is two.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write
the day first. That is the first problem, and its fix is queued. The second is the booking-v3 form:
it prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so people at day-first tenants type the month first.
The parser fix does not touch it. The two were merged because their subject lines match
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Two tickets, one per problem. The parser fix closes only the first. Details:
[three problems under one ticket](/kb/incidents/4471-causes).
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- A big ticket can be several bugs reported many times. Check the cause before you merge, then count
  once per problem.
- Match on cause (tenant locale and booking form), not on subject line.
- Write the page while the queue is still in your head.
